 ((:id "schema/fixed-tables-goal" :type :work-set :children ("packet-wire" "fixed-tables" "variable-tables" "shared" "acceptance-gates" "integration" "message-form-ports" "card-variable-tables"))
  (:id "fixed-tables" :type :roadmap :title "Fixed Tables" :text ("Fixed tables provide versioning such that a new reader can always read an old writer. They are good for messages between the game server and a backend, or the backend and the website where the reader and writer have different versions of the protocol." "This work is on the sprint branch sprint/schema-vt-core and is not yet on main. Cells show ✅ verified complete or ❌ not yet verified complete: a cell is ✅ only when every task under it is done with its acceptance recorded, by the landed cards, in docs/roadmap-evidence/. Built, partial and unstarted states stay in the source data; the [feature survey](docs/FIXED-TABLES-SURVEY.md) records the full scope.") :scope-revision 2 :source-revision
