  (:id "cards/a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus" :type :task :title "Layers L1 and L2 of the card design in C: round-trip and render the shared corpus" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-vt-c" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-vt-c" :tier "pro" :needs ("the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set") :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: layers L1 and L2 of the card design in C: the card record as a generated variable table with an owning facade and the customer bounds, and the brief text parsed once and rendered many times, each matching the Go leg byte for byte on the shared corpus. The facade lives in tables/cards/c (cards.h, cards.c, sha256.c, cards_test.c, driver.c and the executable driver script); its calls are the Go facade calls in the language's own spelling. Done when make cards-c-test runs TestCardRoundTripsThePopulatedFixture, TestCardBoundsRefuseBeforePublishing and TestParseRenderMatchesGo green, make cards-c-conformance reports pass for load, save, render, parse and bounds, and the negative control goes red on render only. Needs: the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set (open). Order: first in line in schema-vt-c; needed by a-c-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus. No attempt was dealt; nothing pushed. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-c (base sprint/schema-finish).")
