  (:id "vt/cs/generator-panic" :type :task :title "C#: a red at the branch head that holds 31 cells" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cstable/fixedform_csunions_test.go: TestGenerateCsUnionsDoesNotPanic" "./bin/schema generate --lang cs --out build/x test/tables/CsUnions.schema exits 0" "guarding only fixedCollectTypes still panics in emitFixedWriteElement at internal/codegen/cstable/fixedform.go:1525, so every arm walk is guarded" "make tables-cs-leg, tables-cs-wire-fuzz, tables-cs-retain-fuzz, tables-cs-view, tables-cook-open-cs, tables-block, tables-block-fuzz") :tested-revision "489f572e6" :note "FIXED at 489f572e6: fixedCollectTypes read v.F.Type before checking v.F, so a payload-free arm (empty in Leaf, signal in Choice) dereferenced nil at fixedform.go:181; the write, slot, and block walks had the same unguarded reads. Every arm walk now skips a nil arm the way cpptable/fixedform.go:280-282 does (a payload-free arm names no type, docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.6). The unit test, ./bin/schema generate --lang cs on test/tables/CsUnions.schema, and the full build/tables-generated-cs/.stamp are RUN green at 489f572e6; the named make targets are the functional gate. With the serialize.cs sibling cloned and dotnet's NuGet migration marker seeded (its MigrationRunner named mutex opens /tmp/.dotnet/shm, which the sandbox denies with EACCES), tables-cs-leg now RUNS and gets past generation, but it fails to COMPILE on a further pre-existing red that is out of this card's scope: string-typed union arms (tables/messages Origin.note string(24)) emit invalid C# (/* ? */)v from csTypeName's fallback (internal/codegen/cstable/codecs.go:56), so build/tables-generated-cs/messages/MessagesTable.cs:7882 is a syntax error. The CsUnions panic itself stays fixed and is held green by TestGenerateCsUnionsDoesNotPanic.")
